   $q$Which statement best explains how the endings differ in the way they present the lesson?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Text 1 leaves the lesson unspoken, while Text 2 ends with Caspian admitting aloud that he was too loud.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-texts"},{"text":"Both texts end with a character announcing the lesson directly to the other performers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-transformation"},{"text":"Text 1 ends with Oriel giving up singing, while Text 2 ends with Caspian quitting the combo.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Text 1 states the lesson as a village saying, while Text 2 leaves it unspoken and shows it only through Caspian's playing.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Text 1 states the lesson as a village saying, while Text 2 leaves it unspoken and shows it only through Caspian's playing.$q$, $q$The legend closes with "The valley says that the echo comes only to those who leave room for it," while Text 2 notes that Caspian never admitted it but "just played" differently. The narrator says Caspian never said he had been too loud, so the admission choice is wrong.$q$, 'draft', 'ef91595a-cd70-58eb-906b-5331fee2fab5')
