   $q$What does the author of Text 2 suggest by replacing the legend's salt with trail information?$q$, $q$[{"text":"That information matters far less than physical goods, so Anjali's effort was mostly for her own benefit.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-theme"},{"text":"That information can be a vital delivery today, and people may rely on it in ways its provider cannot see.","is_correct":true},{"text":"That modern promises are easier to keep than old ones, since websites never require any real effort.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"That trail reports are dangerous to rely on, since the woman almost canceled her visit because of the page.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$That information can be a vital delivery today, and people may rely on it in ways its provider cannot see.$q$, $q$Like the village's salt, the report helps people Anjali "had never met," and the woman's message reveals a need Anjali did not know about. The woman nearly canceled before checking the page, so the page helped her rather than misleading her.$q$, 'draft', '001ee688-f6e0-574b-b339-66b07e59a367')
